---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';

const title = 'About Opus Conservatory';
const description = 'How Opus Conservatory grew from a four-student piano studio into a two-location music school.';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={title} description={description} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main class="container">
			<h1>About Opus Conservatory</h1>

			<p class="lede">
				Recognized as one of the best music schools in Virginia, Opus Conservatory began with four
				students in 2008 as "Brambleton Piano Studio," founded and directed by Marisela Smith, who
				trained at the National Music Conservatory in Caracas, Venezuela and studied under Professor
				Sidonia Stern in Germany. We have worked with more than a thousand students as we've grown
				into the Opus School of Music and Conservatory, now serving students across two Virginia
				studios.
			</p>

			<p>
				We offer individualized beginner, intermediate, and advanced lessons to children as young as
				three and adults, taught by a professional team of classically trained musicians, each with
				years of teaching experience.
			</p>

			<h2>Curriculum</h2>
			<p>
				Our programs are modeled after the Royal Conservatory's Music Development Program, a
				curriculum that provides measurable standards of musical achievement across North America.
				Students advance from one level to the next by completing the program's music requirements
				and being tested by an independent Royal Conservatory assessor — demonstrating both their
				knowledge of music theory and their playing skills. Our tailored lessons cover all the key
				areas of music education: understanding the instrument and developing technical skill, music
				theory and vocabulary, performance skills and recitals, sight-reading, and composition, ear
				training, and improvisation.
			</p>
			<p>
				Weekly lessons run 30, 45, or 60 minutes depending on the age and level of the student.
				Students learn classical pieces, but we can also teach a folk song from their culture or a
				favorite piece from an anime or film — building the skills, technique, and confidence to
				perform in front of an audience at our recitals.
			</p>

			<p>
				Alongside private instruction, we run adaptive lessons for students with disabilities and
				learning differences and a music therapy practice led by a board-certified music therapist.
				Both studios are single-floor and wheelchair accessible, with wide doorways and accessible
				restrooms, so lessons are available to students of every ability. We host recitals twice a
				year and welcome new students of any age with a complimentary trial lesson.
			</p>

			<div class="grid grid-sm">
				<div class="card stat">
					<span class="stat-number">2008</span>
					<span class="stat-label">Founded</span>
				</div>
				<div class="card stat">
					<span class="stat-number">1,000+</span>
					<span class="stat-label">Students taught</span>
				</div>
				<div class="card stat">
					<span class="stat-number">2</span>
					<span class="stat-label">Virginia studios</span>
				</div>
				<div class="card stat">
					<span class="stat-number">10</span>
					<span class="stat-label">Instruments taught</span>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="cluster">
				<a class="button" href="/instructors">Meet our instructors</a>
				<a class="button button-outline" href="/free-trial">Book a free trial</a>
			</div>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	.stat {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		text-align: center;
	}
	.stat-number {
		font-size: 1.75rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		color: var(--accent);
	}
	.stat-label {
		font-size: 0.9rem;
	}
</style>
